  "total": 50,
  "toyota_summary": "China has stopped being a source of easy profit for German automakers and become a threat instead. After decades of delivering massive market share and cash flow, Chinese competitors are now undercutting European manufacturers on price and gaining ground at home. The shift is forcing companies to rethink their entire China strategy—no longer expansion, but survival.\n\nThe industry faces a squeeze from both directions. Chinese rivals are cheaper and increasingly credible on quality. European manufacturers are responding by cutting costs at home, with one major player planning to eliminate 8,000 jobs by the end of 2027, mostly in management and R&D. This creates a vicious cycle: less investment in new technology, slower innovation, further competitive weakness.\n\nWatch whether these job cuts slow innovation enough to matter in the EV transition, where falling behind in the next two years could be fatal.",
